OrionLayer open fix 130 — an injected click is read by the call that drained it
================================================================================

Work order 438 (live re-check of the v2.0.2 move). orion2re on the branch
`orionlayer` (v2.0.2 merged in), after open fix 129. In
src/ext/ext_api.cpp, src/ext/ext_api.h, src/game/fields.cpp,
src/game/platform.cpp and src/game/platform.h; all of it inside
`#ifdef ORION2RE_EXT`.

With the engine window SHOWN, a MSG_INJECT_CLICK was lost about 1 time in 70
(measured: 3 of 300 on the build without this change; the same on v2.0.1).
The click went through the SDL thread: ProcessInput pushed an SDL mouse-down
and mouse-up, the SDL thread turned them into queue events later. The galaxy
map calls Clear_Fields_Above() on every pass; its Mouse_Buffer() pumps the
game's input queue and then clears the flag the pump itself just set, so a
pump that fell between the two halves, or before them, lost the click.

The change. fields::Get_Input sets ext::g_click_direct_ok around its own
ext::Tick (the Tick whose result it reads at once through
Interpret_Mouse_Input). An INJECT_CLICK drained there, one per Tick, is put
into the game's input queue from the game thread: platform::Inject_Game_Click
enqueues the DOWN and the UP (their button states differ, so they are not
coalesced) and sets the present pointer position. Every other Tick (the input
delay's, the screen loop's) and a film take the SDL path as before. The hold
of open fix 129 is taken first, as before.

Live proof: UNVERIFIED beyond the numbers in doc/orion2re_open_fixes.md
entry 130 (Xvfb, no window manager, no real pointer motion).

